# Scene 10: June 2026, what really happened. Starts on its own after scene 9.
# The ending for the meters, then the real Bac 2026 credited to the press, then
# the debrief in the binder, then the last screen. Short mode keeps the ending
# line, three real figures and the debrief.

~ start
do GameState.reveal_dashboard()
if GameState.ending() == "smooth"
	do Story.backdrop("A smooth session")
	Every paper on time, every candidate seated. The region asks for your plan as a template.
elif GameState.ending() == "strained"
	do Story.backdrop("It held, but strained")
	Centre 26 got through. Next year's plan has a few new lines.
else
	do Story.backdrop("The centre made the news")
	A photo of an unsigned envelope is on Facebook by noon.
do Story.backdrop("June 2026, what really happened")
if not GameState.short_mode
	The press: 162,435 candidates registered; more than 20,000 teachers marked the copies in 32 centres.
The press: 955 fraud cases in the main session, about double the year before.
The press: Signal jammers were dropped for good as ineffective; the ministry turned to real-time phone detection.
if GameState.has_flag("bought_tech")
	Si Hédi: Told you. Boxes don't supervise. The machines weren't the answer; trained people were.
if not GameState.short_mode
	The press: Results reached candidates by SMS on 20 June, three days before the announced date.
The press: 35.67% passed the main session, the lowest in five years; 50.72% after the control session.
if GameState.has_flag("metrics_passrate")
	You chose the pass rate as your metric. Your centre didn't control it, and it arrived after your project ended. A metric has to measure your project's performance.
do Story.open_debrief()
do Story.backdrop("", "Your centre's quality plan and staffing plan are done. But who tells the parents? What could still go wrong? Who prints the papers? Over to Team 2.")
=> END
